/-!
# Candidate words for the three native vector orbits

A breadth-first search in the literal ATLAS column generators produces this
parent forest. Roots 1, 4 and 7 represent the three nonzero vector orbits;
zero is its own root. These definitions assert no mathematical result.
`Certificates` checks the roots, strict descent, every edge, and invariance.

Source: Aschbacher–Segev, *The uniqueness of groups of type J₄*, Invent.
Math. 105 (1991), (4.2), p.597, DOI 10.1007/BF01232280. Original matrix
provenance is in the imported native `M22James.Model`.
-/

